    <string name="alerts_now_bar_samsung_help_title">Samsung Now Bar setup</string>
    <string name="alerts_now_bar_developer_options">Developer options</string>
    <string name="alerts_now_bar_samsung_help">For Android Live Updates:\n1. Open Settings &gt; About phone/tablet &gt; Software information.\n2. Tap Build number seven times and confirm your screen lock.\n3. Return to Settings &gt; Developer options.\n4. Turn on Live notifications for all apps.\n5. Make sure Settings &gt; Lock screen and AOD &gt; Now bar is enabled.\n\nIf “Live notifications for all apps” is missing, select Samsung compatibility above. Samsung changes third-party access by model, region, and firmware build even when Android and One UI versions match.\n\nIf both modes remain ordinary notifications, that firmware or device does not expose a third-party Now Bar surface. Codex Meter cannot override Samsung’s system allowlist.</string>

